WEBVTT

00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:14.245
Hatenkou Yugi

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.556
Tabidachi wa sone totsuzen

00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:22.027
Guzen no yona hitsuzen

00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:27.829
Mawari dashita unmei ga kishimu

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:32.268
Totsuzen no ame ni sozen

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:35.706
Furarete zubunure bozen

00:00:35.707 --> 00:00:41.805
Warai tobase michi wa hirakareru

00:00:42.447 --> 00:00:45.616
Muimi na koto ni kakusareteru

00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:49.187
Ichiban daiji na mono wa nani

00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:57.094
Kitto kiseki wa okosu mono waratte

00:00:57.763 --> 00:01:00.596
My Heartbreaking Romance

00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:04.836
Hajikeyo omou mama ni

00:01:04.836 --> 00:01:10.138
Omoshiro yukai sore ga kihon

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:14.171
Kimi no Heartrending Sorrow

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:18.416
Ima wa mada furenai yo

00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:24.879
Mazu wa koko kara hajimeyo

00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:29.992
Am | ever

00:01:38.704 --> 00:01:40.001
Thank you for last night.

00:01:42.007 --> 00:01:44.373
Thanks to you, Vi was safe
without a single scratch.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:47.437
| don’t need your obvious flattery.

00:01:47.846 --> 00:01:49.643
More importantly, there’s something
| need to ask you.

00:01:49.915 --> 00:01:50.847
What would that be?

00:01:51.016 --> 00:01:53.883
What’s your intention? Tell me everything.

00:01:54.386 --> 00:01:59.722
It really bugs me when I’m dragged
into something without knowing all the facts.

00:02:00.726 --> 00:02:04.822
Unknown
Pestination (second Part)

00:02:06.765 --> 00:02:08.357
| guess | have no choice.

00:02:08.867 --> 00:02:15.033
The truth is that Vincent is an illegitimate child
of the King of Obplay and one of his servants.

00:02:15.874 --> 00:02:19.275
Normally, he would have been
disregarded as he is now.

00:02:20.712 --> 00:02:25.411
But there was an epidemic
and all the other heirs perished.

00:02:26.018 --> 00:02:30.546
So Vi was acknowledged
and has become the new heir to the throne.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:36.024
Apparently, that ring was a gift
from the King to the servant.

00:02:36.628 --> 00:02:39.495
You could say that it’s equivalent
to his proof of identity.

00:02:41.166 --> 00:02:45.034
So, that explains why he needs
experts like you to guard him.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.296
Bingo!

00:02:46.738 --> 00:02:49.366
And yet, you’re just leaving him totally unguarded.

00:02:49.508 --> 00:02:54.070
Not to worry. Unlike someone we know,
we won't commit a stupid blunder.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:03:00.985
Stupid blunder? You mean, letting him
almost get kidnapped by some sketchy guys?

00:03:01.453 --> 00:03:04.320
If that’s what you’re implying,
it’s not me. | actually saved him.

00:03:06.224 --> 00:03:08.886
Who cares who’s the klutz?

00:03:09.127 --> 00:03:12.460
In fact, you're both annoying and equally to blame.

00:03:12.898 --> 00:03:16.163
Stop picking a fight with her. She’s just a kid.

00:03:18.036 --> 00:03:19.401
You’re defending her.

00:03:19.805 --> 00:03:21.272
What makes you think so?

00:03:21.606 --> 00:03:23.904
You're also to blame, Hahzel.

00:03:24.242 --> 00:03:27.370
You don’t need to keep your promise
when things go that wrong.

00:03:27.879 --> 00:03:30.541
When your life is in danger,
go ahead and use magic or whatever you can.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:36.450
| appreciate your suggestion,
but I’m not using magic for the next six days.

00:03:37.989 --> 00:03:39.422
| promised, after all.

00:03:39.991 --> 00:03:43.361
Besides, this isn’t my first time doing this.

00:03:43.361 --> 00:03:44.089
Hm’?

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:48.129
My father used to always say...

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:53.630
You never know when or how
you might lose your magical ability.

00:03:53.972 --> 00:03:58.466
So you need to learn to do anything without it.

00:04:01.346 --> 00:04:02.108
Huh?

00:04:05.083 --> 00:04:07.881
Now, do your best to climb down the mountain.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:11.651
All by yourself, with only that outdoor knife.

00:04:13.825 --> 00:04:18.319
If you use magic before you get home,
Dad will hang himself.

00:04:19.197 --> 00:04:23.697
| was suddenly forbidden to use magic
in a pitch-dark area,

00:04:24.035 --> 00:04:28.039
where the compass was useless and some
mysterious spirits were wandering around.

00:04:28.039 --> 00:04:30.371
So | walked towards the foot
of the mountain crying all the way.

00:04:31.676 --> 00:04:36.739
And then, halfway through, | noticed
that he was hiding and watching over me.

00:04:37.415 --> 00:04:39.280
It was so obvious that he was worried.

00:04:42.654 --> 00:04:44.622
What an idiotically doting parent.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:46.582
He really cherishes me.

00:04:47.092 --> 00:04:51.961
You don’t have to pamper me like my father did,
but help me out when | get into trouble, okay?

00:04:52.397 --> 00:04:55.366
And I'll help you when you go through hardship.

00:04:55.834 --> 00:04:57.665
Let’s live strong together, okay?

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.529
Heat-tan? Who is that?

00:05:00.872 --> 00:05:03.340
Is that the person
who used to be friends with Soresta?

00:05:03.675 --> 00:05:07.873
Wow, it’s been already ten years since he died.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.076
Are you denying that | ever existed?

00:05:12.551 --> 00:05:13.916
So you guys are close, huh?

00:05:14.186 --> 00:05:15.016
Of course.

00:05:15.353 --> 00:05:16.581
We're comrades.

00:05:16.855 --> 00:05:20.347
I’m his comrade, not you.

00:05:22.828 --> 00:05:24.489
Don’t you mean “ex-comrade”?

00:05:25.697 --> 00:05:28.598
I’m the one who’s on a journey with Alzeid now.

00:05:33.238 --> 00:05:35.570
Knock it off. Stop acting so immature.

00:05:37.242 --> 00:05:40.109
Man, what a drag.

00:05:46.284 --> 00:05:49.879
It doesn’t look like it will be easy
to separate those two, huh?

00:05:50.088 --> 00:05:53.785
Not a problem. We just have
to change the plan now.

00:05:54.259 --> 00:05:55.453
What do you have in mind?

00:05:56.094 --> 00:06:02.329
We'll remind Alzeid of our old days,
so that we can bring him over to our side.

00:06:04.936 --> 00:06:07.029
You sure that'll work?

00:06:07.505 --> 00:06:08.733
I’m positive.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:13.968
Besides, it looks like there are
other bad guys lying in wait.

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:37.665
Listen up.

00:06:38.069 --> 00:06:41.505
When they run out of the building
fleeing the fire, that’s our chance.

00:06:41.806 --> 00:06:44.900
Once we're surrounded by the smoke,
they can’t tell who’s who.

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:48.436
Oh, | see. What a great strategy.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:53.212
Although, we aren’t that naive
to fall for a ploy like that.

00:06:56.721 --> 00:07:01.215
Too bad, you aren’t the only ones
who are trying to take advantage of Vi.

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:12.964
A fire?

00:07:14.739 --> 00:07:16.036
Vi, wake up!

00:07:20.111 --> 00:07:23.376
C’mon, just keep quiet and give us the kid.

00:07:23.615 --> 00:07:25.583
Vi, hold on tight.

00:07:44.235 --> 00:07:45.725
What the hell?

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:49.672
Alzeid!

00:07:52.143 --> 00:07:54.976
| can’t possibly protect Vi without using magic.

00:07:56.114 --> 00:07:59.174
You don’t need to keep your promise
when things go that wrong.

00:08:00.452 --> 00:08:01.282
So what?

00:08:04.889 --> 00:08:07.858
Jeez, what are Heat-tan and Soresta doing?

00:08:09.427 --> 00:08:11.292
You wanted to see me?

00:08:16.835 --> 00:08:17.927
What took you so long?!

00:08:24.042 --> 00:08:26.340
I’m sorry, Rahzel-chan.

00:08:30.281 --> 00:08:33.273
Wh-why...?

00:08:38.223 --> 00:08:38.848
Rahzel!

00:08:42.027 --> 00:08:42.823
Tsk.

00:08:44.029 --> 00:08:44.757
You’re annoying!

00:08:54.539 --> 00:08:55.733
Isn't this...

00:09:07.118 --> 00:09:09.348
Hey, come on, Newbie!

00:09:09.821 --> 00:09:13.621
This guy right here is betting his life on you!

00:09:15.226 --> 00:09:18.787
Six! Seven! Eight!

00:09:20.498 --> 00:09:24.264
What’s the matter? Your legs are all shaky.

00:09:26.071 --> 00:09:26.696
What?!

00:09:27.772 --> 00:09:28.602
Dammit!

00:09:31.042 --> 00:09:31.667
Huh?!

00:09:32.177 --> 00:09:33.906
How come my punches aren’t landing?

00:09:50.495 --> 00:09:51.723
Did you see that, Al-kiddo?

00:09:52.063 --> 00:09:56.563
He was using the string to manipulate
his opponent without being noticed.

00:09:56.801 --> 00:09:57.631
Yeah.

00:09:58.670 --> 00:10:00.228
He’s skillful, huh?

00:10:08.446 --> 00:10:09.572
It’s a trap...

00:10:10.849 --> 00:10:15.786
Yeah, looks like Soresta
is handling things smoothly.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:21.014
Well, I'll do my best to meet your expectations.

00:10:21.526 --> 00:10:22.754
I’m counting on you.

00:10:26.397 --> 00:10:27.694
Wh-where am |’?

00:10:29.467 --> 00:10:30.661
Thank goodness.

00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:33.903
Oh yeah, Rahzel...

00:10:34.339 --> 00:10:35.135
Where is she?

00:10:45.416 --> 00:10:47.145
Wh-what should | do?

00:10:51.356 --> 00:10:52.755
Say "ah."

00:10:52.957 --> 00:10:54.117
Ah...

00:10:54.659 --> 00:10:56.427
Ow!

00:10:56.427 --> 00:10:58.895
You can't fool me with that
rabbit-shaped apple!

00:10:59.664 --> 00:11:03.191
You better do something
about this awkward position you put me in!

00:11:03.868 --> 00:11:05.665
And what happened to Vi anyway?

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:08.234
Why would you guys kidnap him?

00:11:08.439 --> 00:11:10.202
Weren't you supposed to be his bodyguards?

00:11:10.909 --> 00:11:14.777
Even if | tell you, what could you do
in that position you're in?

00:11:17.549 --> 00:11:22.851
| wonder what Alzeid sees in this helpless kid?

00:11:23.555 --> 00:11:26.457
It’s not like she’s sexually appealing.

00:11:26.457 --> 00:11:30.086
In order to be his comrade,
why would | need to be sexually attractive?

00:11:30.261 --> 00:11:32.058
Stop having dirty thoughts.

00:11:32.764 --> 00:11:35.892
Who says men and women can’t have
non-romantic relationships?

00:11:36.034 --> 00:11:37.934
You must be sexually frustrated.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:48.240
That was mean, Rahzel-chan.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.174
Yeah, | just made him shut up.

00:11:51.549 --> 00:11:52.777
It kind of felt good.

00:11:54.052 --> 00:12:02.357
Knowing Alzeid, he’d probably never say it,
but | think he really cares about you and Soresta.

00:12:03.394 --> 00:12:07.592
The three of you must have shared
lots of experiences before | met you,

00:12:08.132 --> 00:12:10.293
but | feel stupid for being so jealous.

00:12:10.735 --> 00:12:12.259
You're softhearted, huh?

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:13.604
Thanks.

00:12:13.605 --> 00:12:14.970
That wasn’t a compliment.

00:12:15.506 --> 00:12:19.306
But | love the naive side of you, Rahzel-chan.

00:12:21.145 --> 00:12:23.670
And yet, | am on the other side this time.

00:12:24.482 --> 00:12:29.044
You’re so cold. You prefer
your old boyfriend over me?

00:12:29.287 --> 00:12:32.313
Will you stop making that misleading remark?

00:12:32.991 --> 00:12:36.984
Sorry. Just be patient until Al-kiddo shows up.

00:12:54.812 --> 00:12:58.179
| shouldn’t have made the promise
not to use magic.

00:13:08.293 --> 00:13:12.229
| guess this hand won’t be useful for a while.

00:13:13.364 --> 00:13:15.195
Want me to quietly wait for help?

00:13:15.533 --> 00:13:17.364
Don’t patronize me.

00:13:17.835 --> 00:13:20.395
Don’t use magic no matter what.

00:13:22.307 --> 00:13:23.331
Deal?

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.545
Now, let’s fight to the death.

00:13:29.547 --> 00:13:30.104
Vi!

00:13:30.581 --> 00:13:31.481
Vi!

00:13:31.482 --> 00:13:32.471
He’s not here.

00:13:35.353 --> 00:13:36.012
Not here.

00:13:37.088 --> 00:13:38.020
Not here, either!

00:13:38.456 --> 00:13:39.388
Vi!

00:13:39.957 --> 00:13:40.855
Vi!

00:13:43.828 --> 00:13:44.852
Is this...

00:13:45.096 --> 00:13:46.620
Let go! Let me go!

00:13:47.498 --> 00:13:47.998
Vi!

00:13:47.999 --> 00:13:49.523
Let me go!

00:13:49.934 --> 00:13:52.703
You’re surprisingly brave for a prince.

00:13:52.704 --> 00:13:55.506
Shut up! | need to save Rahzel!

00:13:55.506 --> 00:13:58.675
Relax. Rahzel-chan’s safe—

00:13:58.676 --> 00:13:59.802
I’m right here!

00:14:03.114 --> 00:14:04.547
Nice catch!

00:14:05.983 --> 00:14:07.416
Oh, oops.

00:14:07.585 --> 00:14:09.620
We're enemies right now, aren’t we?

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.814
It just slipped my mind.

00:14:10.955 --> 00:14:12.513
Talk about being a fool.

00:14:13.324 --> 00:14:14.154
Rahzel!

00:14:14.359 --> 00:14:15.121
Dammit!

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:16.424
Rahzel!

00:14:16.761 --> 00:14:18.353
Vi, ’'m glad you’re safe.

00:14:18.563 --> 00:14:19.461
Yeah.

00:14:19.664 --> 00:14:22.326
But the biggest hurdle starts from here.

00:14:23.134 --> 00:14:29.369
Unfortunately, even with magic
or some dirty tricks, | doubt | could defeat him.

00:14:34.045 --> 00:14:39.347
Crossing swords like this reminds me
of the time when we first met.

00:14:42.487 --> 00:14:48.392
At that duel back then, | wondered
what kind of man would bet his life on me.

00:14:49.527 --> 00:14:50.926
But you were...

00:14:53.264 --> 00:14:53.897
Wait!

00:14:53.898 --> 00:14:55.024
Just wait up!

00:14:56.701 --> 00:14:57.793
Who are you?

00:14:58.536 --> 00:14:59.798
| don’t remember any of that.

00:15:00.104 --> 00:15:01.537
But | do!

00:15:03.241 --> 00:15:06.039
Man, what the hell did you do?

00:15:06.277 --> 00:15:09.644
You dislocated your hand yourself.

00:15:10.248 --> 00:15:14.344
The Princess should’ve just waited
for The Prince to rescue her.

00:15:14.786 --> 00:15:16.981
Relying on others isn’t my thing.

00:15:17.388 --> 00:15:19.083
Listen carefully.

00:15:19.257 --> 00:15:22.090
There’s a great old saying:

00:15:22.527 --> 00:15:24.017
“In the character for ‘person,’

00:15:24.495 --> 00:15:27.396
the guy on the left is clearly leaning
on the one on the right!”

00:15:27.832 --> 00:15:28.730
Huh?

00:15:28.933 --> 00:15:31.769
Isn’t that supposed to be "they’re
both supporting each other"?

00:15:31.769 --> 00:15:33.327
What kind of nonsense are you mumbling?

00:15:33.538 --> 00:15:37.304
The length of the left and right are clearly different,
so there’s no way it could be equal!

00:15:37.842 --> 00:15:41.212
If ’'m not tall enough to support the other,
lll rise as high as | possibly can.

00:15:41.212 --> 00:15:47.981
No matter how reckless it may seem,
ll move forward with my unflinching determination.

00:15:48.519 --> 00:15:51.147
I’m not dealing
with some ordinary guys, you know.

00:15:52.523 --> 00:15:54.150
You aren’t gonna beg for your life?

00:15:54.659 --> 00:15:56.889
I'd rather die laughing.

00:16:03.067 --> 00:16:04.735
You heard her. Sorry.

00:16:04.735 --> 00:16:06.896
This side seems more fun, after all.

00:16:07.371 --> 00:16:10.173
I’m back to being Rahzel-chan’s ally.

00:16:10.174 --> 00:16:11.505
Huh?!

00:16:12.276 --> 00:16:13.800
What do you think you're doing?!

00:16:14.078 --> 00:16:16.580
Are you going to disobey
Commander Soresta’s order?

00:16:16.581 --> 00:16:17.748
You sure you wanna fight?

00:16:17.748 --> 00:16:20.317
Fine by me, but just so you know,
I’m super strong.

00:16:20.318 --> 00:16:22.650
Bullshit! Stop talking nonsense. You're unarmed!

00:16:23.855 --> 00:16:24.981
Unarmed?

00:16:27.758 --> 00:16:29.817
Bring it on, boys.

00:16:30.528 --> 00:16:33.656
lll make you feel so good
that your synapses will get burned out.

00:16:39.804 --> 00:16:42.773
Yeah, that’s right. Don’t you remember?

00:16:43.774 --> 00:16:48.274
The smell of blood... The sensation
of cutting through bones and flesh!

00:16:48.579 --> 00:16:50.376
Everything that makes your heart quiver.

00:16:50.548 --> 00:16:53.449
The battlefield is the only place for us to live.

00:16:53.818 --> 00:16:57.914
And yet, the conflicts and civil wars
in our nation have been suppressed,

00:16:58.256 --> 00:17:00.656
so there’s nothing left for me!

00:17:01.993 --> 00:17:05.258
Is that why you attempted
a coup d’etat using The Prince?

00:17:05.463 --> 00:17:08.296
That way, | can regain everything.

00:17:10.368 --> 00:17:14.532
You understand, don’t you?
| want us to go back to the old days...

00:17:15.006 --> 00:17:16.030
Together...

00:17:17.875 --> 00:17:19.365
Together with you!

00:17:20.311 --> 00:17:23.940
Damn, you're a freak.

00:17:31.389 --> 00:17:36.292
I’m sorry to disappoint you,
but | have no interest in the battlefield.

00:17:36.694 --> 00:17:41.529
| don’t feel any pain,
let alone joy in killing people.

00:17:42.733 --> 00:17:46.396
Soresta... even if it’s you.

00:17:48.005 --> 00:17:50.872
I’m no longer his comrade, huh?

00:17:51.309 --> 00:17:52.742
Do you have any last words?

00:17:53.444 --> 00:17:54.502
No.

00:17:55.246 --> 00:17:56.110
See ya.

00:17:59.483 --> 00:18:02.509
Are you trying to save me?

00:18:03.421 --> 00:18:04.786
You should sing my praises.

00:18:05.323 --> 00:18:08.258
I’m still obeying the ban on magic.

00:18:08.659 --> 00:18:10.149
That’s the way it should be.

00:18:11.062 --> 00:18:13.292
| guess. That’s how it should be, huh?

00:18:14.966 --> 00:18:15.898
Yeah.

00:18:17.301 --> 00:18:18.791
Let’s head back, then.

00:18:19.003 --> 00:18:20.129
Yeah, let’s go!

00:18:21.038 --> 00:18:22.403
Vi and Heat-tan, too.

00:18:23.507 --> 00:18:25.839
There you go. Good luck.

00:18:26.544 --> 00:18:28.808
Wh-why?

00:18:29.513 --> 00:18:30.775
Why is it?

00:18:30.982 --> 00:18:34.782
Alzeid... Why have you forgotten?

00:18:35.486 --> 00:18:37.147
| don’t remember any of that.

00:18:37.588 --> 00:18:38.612
Why?

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:40.416
That’s...

00:18:40.891 --> 00:18:41.789
That’s...

00:18:42.193 --> 00:18:44.627
That was supposed to be my place!

00:18:48.733 --> 00:18:51.395
Try to remember, Alzeid!

00:18:52.136 --> 00:18:53.034
Rahzel!

00:18:55.239 --> 00:18:55.967
Wait!

00:18:57.441 --> 00:18:58.703
Just wait up!

00:18:59.844 --> 00:19:03.473
|... | want to be friends with you.

00:19:03.748 --> 00:19:09.311
If not, ’'ll do your cleaning duty
or get food for you.

00:19:10.655 --> 00:19:11.587
So...

00:19:11.922 --> 00:19:13.023
So, please...

00:19:13.024 --> 00:19:17.222
Wait, you want to be my gofer?

00:19:18.029 --> 00:19:19.462
What a weirdo.

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:27.296
Perhaps, what | wanted
might have been in my hand all along.

00:19:27.838 --> 00:19:32.468
It’s just that | didn’t realize it until too late.

00:19:54.098 --> 00:19:55.395
Now...

00:19:55.866 --> 00:19:58.426
| wonder how HE will react.

00:20:15.486 --> 00:20:18.250
What’s wrong, Idiot?

00:20:20.658 --> 00:20:21.992
Here’s your umbrella.

00:20:21.992 --> 00:20:24.620
You should’ve come sooner.

00:20:25.196 --> 00:20:28.654
But you looked like you were crying.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:32.626
You’re the one who’s crying.

00:20:43.147 --> 00:20:44.842
| was being a bit arrogant.

00:20:46.016 --> 00:20:47.779
| thought | could do anything on my own.

00:20:48.819 --> 00:20:55.383
Instead of always being protected,
| thought | could do something for others.

00:20:56.827 --> 00:21:01.924
But | don’t even know
how to say thank you or sorry.

00:21:08.706 --> 00:21:10.105
I’m helpless...

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:19.247
...and without being allowed to resist,
my journey is about to end.

00:21:31.829 --> 00:21:32.887
Dad...?

00:21:43.674 --> 00:21:47.344
Tonari no heya kara

00:21:47.344 --> 00:21:50.973
Waraigoe ga suru

00:21:51.148 --> 00:21:58.350
Ussura mezameru asa ga konna ni Itoshii

00:21:58.722 --> 00:22:05.958
Dokoka de yumemita ichimai no e ni wa

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:13.534
Mou anata no isu wo kakitashita bakari da yo

00:22:13.704 --> 00:22:18.204
Kanashii monogatari ga ima

00:22:20.644 --> 00:22:29.348
Curtain no mukogawa machibuse shite itemo

00:22:31.355 --> 00:22:38.591
Ashita ni wa mishiranu hito no yoni nattemo

00:22:38.863 --> 00:22:45.996
Anata ga koko ni iru tashika na kiseki wo shinjite

00:22:46.303 --> 00:22:53.641
Sashidasareta te ni wa wakare no yokan mo naku

00:22:53.978 --> 00:23:01.714
Tada dakishimetakute ima ruisen ga yurunda
